    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.ai\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nWhen the tags in an xml file contain underscores, the selection is not correct.\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\n0.9.2\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. Open an xml file, containing the following line: `<first_name>First Name</first_name>`\r\n2. Move the cursor to any position inside the `<first_name>` tag \r\n3. Press `vit`\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nThe text between the pair of tags gets selected: `First Name`\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nError message:\r\n`(mini.ai) No textobject \"it\" found covering region within 500 lines and `search_method = 'cover_or_next'`.`",
