            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> That said, I don't think I am the right person to offer a good PR to the `nvim-treesitter-textobjects` plugin.\r\n> I have no in-depth knowledge regarding the plugin and `treesitter`'s query syntax.\r\n\r\nIf you indulge a small inspirational talk, then I'd like to point out that no one has as in-depth knowledge about tree-sitter queries without trying. Most of those queries are results of actual language users being persistent enough to sit and try to \"fake it till you make it\". Looking at other queries, reading a bit about how they work in general (I started [here](https://tree-sitter.github.io/tree-sitter/using-parsers#query-syntax)) and playing with them interactively (like with Neovim's built-in `:InspectTree` and `:PreviewQuery` in latest Nightly) goes a long way. Otherwise, if nobody is invested enough, chances are that it won't be done at all.",
